# TwoTrianglesSharingVertex.obj - converted from CGAL 6.2's own PMP_Mesh_repair test fixture
# (PMP_Mesh_repair/test/PMP_Mesh_repair/data-repair/two_triangles_sharing_a_vertex.off, used by
# test_pmp_manifoldness.cpp's test_pinched_triangles<>() case). Trivial 5-point/2-triangle
# geometry, converted here for licensing-safety reasons (see the assistant's note on
# ThreeTrianglesSharingVertex.obj) rather than redistributing the .off directly.
#
# Two disconnected triangles - (1,2,5) and (2,3,4) below - meeting ONLY at vertex 2 (1,0,0), no
# shared edge: CGAL's own canonical minimal non-manifold vertex, the same pattern
# RepairMeshTest.obj's bowtie region uses embedded in a larger composite scene. Kept here as an
# isolated file so its repair result can be compared directly against
# ThreeTrianglesSharingVertex.obj's 3-way fan: duplicate_non_manifold_vertices() should report
# exactly 1 vertex created for this 2-way case, vs 2 for the 3-way one (N-1 splits for an N-way
# fan).

mtllib TwoTrianglesSharingVertex.mtl
usemtl mat_1

v 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 1.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 2.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 2.000000 1.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 1.000000 0.000000

f 1 2 5
f 2 3 4
